        {
          "es": "Entonces, al atardecer, empieza el ruido.",
          "en": "Then, at sunset, the noise begins."
        },
        {
          "es": "La gente golpea tambores, gongs y ollas, y recorre las calles con antorchas encendidas.",
          "en": "People bang drums, gongs and pots, and carry flaming torches through the streets."
        },
        {
          "es": "Los jóvenes pasean monstruos gigantes de bambú y papel, llamados ogoh-ogoh.",
          "en": "Young people parade giant monsters of bamboo and paper, called ogoh-ogoh."
        },
        {
          "es": "Cada barrio arma el suyo durante semanas, y algunos son tan altos como una casa.",
          "en": "Each neighborhood builds its own for weeks, and some are as tall as a house."
        },
        {
          "es": "Son una costumbre moderna, de hace pocas décadas, y al final de la noche muchos se queman.",
          "en": "They are a modern custom, only a few decades old, and at the end of the night many of them are burned."
        }
